# Session Rule (Cursor)

The process is defined in `docs/agent/` — this rule only enforces session start/end. Do not restate the pipeline here.

## Start

1. Read `.agent/project_config.md`, then `.agent/workflow_state.md`.
2. If either is missing or unreadable, stop and ask the user.
3. If a locked slice has an open blocker, report it and ask before proceeding.

## During

- **WIP = 1.** Never lock a second slice while one is active and not `done`.
- Follow `docs/agent/README.md` (stages) and `docs/agent/classes.md` (weight gates).
- Remediation cap is **3**, then human. Never self-approve a `write-security` design.
- Out-of-scope work goes to `.agent/follow-ups/`.
- If the human jumps ahead (build/lock/run with no decision log or approved backlog), redirect using the stage exits + Recovery guards in `docs/agent/README.md`. Guide to the missing stage; do not invent a parallel process.

## End

Update `.agent/workflow_state.md` per `docs/agent/schemas/workflow_state.md`.
